cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "hmm-regime: walk-forward Gaussian HMM market regime detection with causal forward filtering"
version: "0.2.1"
date-released: "2026-11-25"   # the day the GitHub release is published
authors:
  - family-names: "Altekin"
    given-names: "Mehmet Ömer"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-9592-3429"   # optional; remove the # and fill in
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mehmetoaltekin/hmm-regime-detection"
repository-artifact: "https://pypi.org/project/hmm-regime/"
abstract: >-
  Walk-forward Gaussian hidden Markov model for market regime detection. The model is
  re-calibrated on a rolling training window, and regimes are inferred with a causal forward
  filter only, so the probabilities of a day use data up to that day. States are labelled by
  variance, and the number of regimes can be selected per window with AIC or BIC. Python
  package hmm_regime (PyPI: hmm-regime) with a look-ahead invariance test suite.
keywords:
  - hidden markov model
  - regime detection
  - walk-forward
  - volatility
  - quantitative finance
